### Disable tempfile cleanup (Rust)

Source: https://context7.com/stebalien/tempfile/llms.txt

Shows how to disable automatic cleanup of a temporary file using keep(), converting it to a permanent file while maintaining the original path. Useful for debugging or inspection purposes.

```rust
use tempfile::NamedTempFile;
use std::io::Write;

fn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {
    let mut tmpfile = NamedTempFile::new()?;
    writeln!(tmpfile, "Debug output for inspection")?;

    // Disable cleanup and get path
    let path = tmpfile.keep()?;

    println!("File kept at: {:?}", path);
    // File will NOT be deleted automatically

    // Manual cleanup for demo
    std::fs::remove_file(&path)?;
    Ok(())
}
```

