### Multi-Process File Coordination with Locks in Rust

Source: https://context7.com/al8n/fs4-rs/llms.txt

Demonstrates coordinating access between multiple processes or threads using file locks. The `fs4` crate's `FileExt` trait provides `try_lock_exclusive` for acquiring locks with retries. This example uses `std::fs::OpenOptions` and `std::thread` for concurrency.

```rust
use fs4::fs_std::FileExt;
use std::fs::OpenOptions;
use std::io::Write;
use std::time::Duration;
use std::thread;

fn worker(id: usize) -> std::io::Result<()> {
    let file = OpenOptions::new()
        .read(true)
        .write(true)
        .create(true)
        .open("shared.log")?;

    // Try to acquire lock, retry if busy
    loop {
        match file.try_lock_exclusive() {
            Ok(true) => break,
            Ok(false) => {
                println!("Worker {} waiting for lock", id);
                thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(100));
            },
            Err(e) => return Err(e),
        }
    }

    // Critical section - exclusive access guaranteed
    let mut file = file; // Make mutable
    writeln!(&mut file, "Worker {} writing", id)?;
    file.unlock()?;

    Ok(())
}

// Spawn multiple workers
let handles: Vec<_> = (0..5)
    .map(|id| thread::spawn(move || worker(id)))
    .collect();

for handle in handles {
    handle.join().unwrap()?;
}
```

--------------------------------

### Synchronous File Locking with Rust's std::fs::File

Source: https://context7.com/al8n/fs4-rs/llms.txt

Demonstrates synchronous advisory file locking (exclusive and shared) and pre-allocation using the `fs4::fs_std::FileExt` trait for `std::fs::File`. It requires opening files with appropriate read/write permissions and handles lock acquisition, operation, and release. Supports non-blocking lock attempts.

```rust
use fs4::fs_std::FileExt;
use std::fs::OpenOptions;

// Create or open a file with read/write permissions
let file = OpenOptions::new()
    .read(true)
    .write(true)
    .create(true)
    .open("data.txt")?;

// Acquire exclusive lock (blocks until available)
file.lock_exclusive()?;

// Perform operations on locked file
// ... write operations ...

// Release the lock
file.unlock()?;

// Try non-blocking shared lock
let file2 = OpenOptions::new().read(true).open("data.txt")?;
match file2.try_lock_shared() {
    Ok(true) => {
        println!("Lock acquired");
        // ... read operations ...
        file2.unlock()?;
    },
    Ok(false) => println!("File is currently locked"),
    Err(e) => eprintln!("Error: {}", e),
}
```

--------------------------------

### Lock Contention Error Handling in Rust

Source: https://context7.com/al8n/fs4-rs/llms.txt

Shows how to handle lock contention errors specifically, using `fs4::lock_contended_error` to identify platform-specific errors. This allows for robust error management when dealing with concurrent file access. It utilizes `std::fs::OpenOptions` and `FileExt` from `fs4`.

```rust
use fs4::{fs_std::FileExt, lock_contended_error};
use std::fs::OpenOptions;
use std::io::ErrorKind;

let file1 = OpenOptions::new()
    .read(true)
    .write(true)
    .create(true)
    .open("test.txt")?;

let file2 = OpenOptions::new()
    .read(true)
    .open("test.txt")?;

file1.lock_exclusive()?;

// Check for specific lock contention error
match file2.try_lock_shared() {
    Ok(false) => println!("Lock contended - file is locked"),
    Ok(true) => println!("Lock acquired"),
    Err(e) if e.kind() == lock_contended_error().kind() => {
        println!("Detected lock contention error");
    },
    Err(e) => eprintln!("Other error: {}", e),
}

file1.unlock()?;
```

--------------------------------

### Asynchronous File Locking with async-std

Source: https://context7.com/al8n/fs4-rs/llms.txt

Illustrates asynchronous file locking and allocation using `fs4::async_std::AsyncFileExt` with `async_std::fs::File`. This implementation mirrors the Tokio version's API, providing synchronous lock operations and asynchronous allocation/query methods. It requires the `async-std` runtime.

```rust
use fs4::async_std::AsyncFileExt;
use async_std::fs::OpenOptions;

#[async_std::main]
async fn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {
    let file = OpenOptions::new()
        .write(true)
        .create(true)
        .open("async_std_data.txt")
        .await?;

    // Try non-blocking exclusive lock
    if file.try_lock_exclusive()? {
        file.allocate(512 * 1024).await?; // 512KB
        file.unlock_async().await?;
    }

    Ok(())
}
```

--------------------------------

### fs-err Integration for Enhanced Error Reporting in Rust

Source: https://context7.com/al8n/fs4-rs/llms.txt

Integrates `fs4` with `fs-err` for enhanced error reporting, including path information in error messages. This applies to both synchronous and asynchronous (tokio) operations. It requires `fs4`, `fs-err`, and optionally `tokio`.

```rust
// With fs-err v3
use fs4::fs_err3::FileExt;
use fs_err::OpenOptions;

let file = OpenOptions::new()
    .write(true)
    .create(true)
    .open("data.txt")?;

file.lock_exclusive()?;
file.allocate(1024)?;
file.unlock()?;

// With fs-err v3 tokio
use fs4::fs_err3_tokio::AsyncFileExt;
use fs_err::tokio::OpenOptions;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {
    let file = OpenOptions::new()
        .write(true)
        .create(true)
        .open("async_data.txt")
        .await?;

    file.lock_exclusive()?;
    file.allocate(2048).await?;
    file.unlock_async().await?;

    Ok(())
}
```

